CM k9ay-shaped NT probe, CELL form (momwire#456 phase C).  A GX 2 100 is still
CM live at GE, so nec2c fills and factors one 13-segment cell -- and the NT
CM below addresses tag 1 (in the cell) and tag 2 (in the cell).  What this
CM deck measures is whether a network card obeys the SYMMETRIC CELL RULE the
CM way LD does (replicated onto every copy) or is EXEMPT the way EX is
CM (attached once, exactly as addressed).  Its twin k9ay_nt_naive.deck is the
CM same structure written out as four GW cards with the SAME ONE card; the
CM two answer identically on the oracle, so the answer is: exempt.
